<title>USA: Arris in venture with Merck.</title>
<headline>Arris in venture with Merck.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTH SAN FRANCISCO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arris Pharmaceutical Corp said it signed a collaborative research agreement with Merck and Co Inc for the development of a protease inhibitor to counter osteoporosis.</p>
<p>Protease inhibitors work by halting the function of protease, or proteins that bind with other proteins to set in motion various bodily or disease functions.</p>
<p>In the case of the degenerative bone disease osteoporosis, the proteases involved in the process of breaking down the bone outpace those that regenerate it, resulting in the loss of bone mass.</p>
</text>
